cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "StormShield-AI: radar late fusion on nuScenes, an inference-only measurement"
authors:
  - family-names: Algharibeh
    given-names: Moath
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-10-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/algharibeh/StormShield-AI"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - sensor fusion
  - late fusion
  - radar
  - lidar
  - 3d object detection
  - nuscenes
  - degraded sensing
abstract: >-
  Inference-only measurement of what automotive radar adds to LiDAR plus camera
  3D object detection on nuScenes, as the evaluation groundwork for
  StormShield-AI, a design for decision-level fusion with condition-dependent
  sensor trust scoring. Two public pretrained detectors are run unchanged,
  radar returns are associated to their boxes by geometry, and the fused
  results are scored with the official nuScenes devkit across four
  experiments: daytime, night and rain, sparser LiDAR, and LiDAR without a
  usable velocity estimate. Radar velocity fusion leaves mAP unchanged and
  lowers far-range velocity error by about 5 percent with a healthy LiDAR and
  by a third to two fifths when the LiDAR cannot measure velocity. nuScenes
  (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) is not redistributed; the detector checkpoints are from
  MMDetection3D (Apache 2.0).
